{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Added a public startup-override model in [crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs) with explicit startup preset enums for substrate, plants, light, and heater, plus `seeded_state_with_full_overrides(...)` so the TUI and scenario materialization path use the same override contract.\n- Extended the startup flow in [crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs) to expose source water, substrate, plants, filter, light, heater, aeration, and shrimp count, and made scenario changes reset all override fields back to that scenario’s template defaults.\n- Added `AnimalState::with_adults(...)` in [crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs) and a new integration test in [crates/tank_scenarios/tests/startup_overrides.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/tests/startup_overrides.rs) covering heater enablement, adult shrimp seeding, and source-water replacement.\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- Scenario startup defaults are currently hardcoded in [crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs) rather than stored in scenario TOML, because the existing preset schema does not define hardware or stocking template fields. The behavior matches the feature requirement, but the defaults are code-driven for now.\n- The startup light control remains a photoperiod preset selector only; it does not add a separate light on/off toggle, because the spec only required selectable photoperiod presets.\n\n## Testing\n- Ran `cargo fmt --all`.\n- Ran `cargo test --workspace`.\n- Verification required an explicit Nix toolchain path because `cargo` and `cc` were not on the default `PATH` in this shell.\n\n---"}}
